From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:36:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: eliza: enable the APSS watchdog

XBL hands over with the non-secure APSS watchdog running and a 30 s
bite. On the stock software stack the hypervisor services it; with
U-Boot as the next stage nothing does, so the board resets about 30 s
after U-Boot starts, at a prompt, in a fastboot session, or in an OS
that has not taken the watchdog over by then. On the Eliza CQS EVK a
Linux boot with memtest=4 stops in early_memtest 29 s after U-Boot
started and comes back through a watchdog reset.

The Eliza DT describes the watchdog with status "reserved". Enable it
in the U-Boot fragment of the MTP and the CQS EVK so that the qcom_wdt
driver probes it at init and stops it; an OS that wants it restarts it.
With this change the same memtest=4 boot on the EVK runs to the end.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/arm/dts/eliza-u-boot.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/eliza-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/eliza-u-boot.dtsi
index 1c96428bb1c..f0edd8ccb21 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/eliza-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/eliza-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -16,3 +16,11 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * XBL leaves the APSS watchdog running with a 30 s bite and nothing
+ * services it until the OS does: let the qcom_wdt driver probe and stop it.
+ */
+&apss_watchdog {
+	status = "okay";
+};
